A minimal test crate for rustdoc JSON testing

Modules

  ◦ [generics](https://docs.rs/fixture-crate/0.1.0/fixture_crate/generics/index.html) 
    Generic-syntax edge cases, gathered here so signature rendering has a fixture
    for every shape rustdoc JSON can produce. [...]

  ◦ [implementors](https://docs.rs/fixture-crate/0.1.0/fixture_crate/implementors/index.html) 
    Implementor shapes for the trait-page "Implementors" section, mirroring the 
    trillium::Handler family of impls: bounds must surface in the rendering whether
    they're declared inline or in where predicates, and wherever the implementing
    type puts the param — a tuple element, an array element with a const-generic
    length, a bare function-like generic, or nested too deep for inline display.

